"[2304.10399] Nielsen realization in dimension four and projective twists (https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.10399)\nciteturn3view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.10399\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 162\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Geometric Topology\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 20 Apr 2023 (cite5†v1 ), last revised 11 Oct 2023 (this version, v3)]\nL9: # Title:Nielsen realization in dimension four and projective twists\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Mihail Arabadji , cite7†R. Inanc Baykur L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Nielsen realization in dimension four and projective twists, by Mihail Arabadji and 1 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite8†View PDF cite9†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:We demonstrate the existence of numerous non-spin 4-manifolds for which the smooth Nielsen realization problem fails; namely, there exist finite subgroups of their mapping class groups that cannot be realized by any group of diffeomorphisms. This extends and complements recent results for spin 4-manifolds. Our examples span virtually all possible intersection forms, both even and odd, indefinite and definite, and include many irreducible 4-manifolds.\nL17: To derive these examples, we study multi-twists, projective twists, and multi-reflections, which are all mapping classes supported around collections of embedded spheres and projective planes. Our obstructions to Nielsen realization are based on the work of Konno. We investigate projective twists in further detail, and notably, employ them to show that, for many closed symplectic 4-manifolds, the symplectic Torelli group is not generated by squared Dehn twists.\nL18: Comments:  | 21 pages. This version has a revised title and abstract; the content is the same\nL19: Subjects:  | Geometric Topology (math.GT); Differential Geometry (math.DG)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite10†arXiv:2304.10399 [math.GT]\nL21:    | (or cite11†arXiv:2304.10399v3 [math.GT] for this version)\nL22:    | cite12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2304.10399†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Mihail Arabadji [cite13†view email ]\nL26: cite5†[v1] Thu, 20 Apr 2023 15:36:26 UTC (20 KB)\nL27: cite14†[v2] Wed, 7 Jun 2023 14:37:10 UTC (21 KB)\nL28: [v3] Wed, 11 Oct 2023 19:48:17 UTC (22 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled Nielsen realization in dimension four and projective twists, by Mihail Arabadji and 1 other authors\nL35: \nL36:   * cite8†View PDF L37:   * cite9†HTML (experimental) L38:   * cite15†TeX Source L39: \nL40: cite16†view license L41: ### Current browse context:\nL42: \nL43: math.GT\nL44: \nL45: cite17†< prev |   cite18†next > L46: \nL47: cite19†new | cite20†recent | cite21†2023-04 L48: \nL49: Change to browse by:\nL50: \nL51: cite22†math L52: cite23†math.DG L53: \nL54: ### References & Citations\nL55: \nL56:   * cite24†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L57:   * cite25†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L58:   * cite26†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L59: \nL60: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL61: \nL62: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL63: \nL64: [Button: ×]\nL65: \nL66: loading...\nL67: \nL68: Data provided by:\nL69: \nL70: ### Bookmark\nL71: \nL72: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL73: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL74: \nL75: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL76: \nL77: Bibliographic Explorer (cite27†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL78: \nL79: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL80: \nL81: Connected Papers (cite28†What is Connected Papers?†www.connectedpapers.com )\nL82: \n