View a PDF of the paper titled Equivariant Poincar\\'e duality for cyclic groups of prime order and the Nielsen realisation problem, by Kaif Hilman and 2 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite8†View PDF cite9†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:In this companion article to [HKK24], we apply the theory of equivariant Poincaré duality developed there in the special case of cyclic groups $C_p$ of prime order to remove, in a special case, a technical condition given by Davis--Lück [DL24] in their work on the Nielsen realisation problem for aspherical manifolds.\nL17: Along the way, we will also give a complete characterisation of $C_p$--Poincaré spaces as well as introduce a genuine equivariant refinement of the classical notion of virtual Poincaré duality groups which might be of independent interest.\nL18: Comments:  | 30 pages. Comments welcome!\nL19: Subjects:  | Algebraic Topology (math.AT); Geometric Topology (math.GT)\nL20: Report number:  | MPIM-Bonn-2024\nL21: Cite as:  | cite10†arXiv:2409.02220 [math.AT]\nL22:    | (or cite11†arXiv:2409.02220v1 [math.AT] for this version)\nL23:    | cite12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2409.02220†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Dominik Kirstein [cite13†view email ]\nL27: [v1] Tue, 3 Sep 2024 18:44:42 UTC (598 KB)\nL28: \nL29: Full-text links:\nL30: \nL31: ## Access Paper:\nL32: \nL33: View a PDF of the paper titled Equivariant Poincar\\'e duality for cyclic groups of prime order and the Nielsen realisation problem, by Kaif Hilman and 2 other authors\nL34: \nL35:   * cite8†View PDF L36:   * cite9†HTML (experimental) L37:   * cite14†TeX Source L38: \nL39: cite15†view license†creativecommons.org L40: ### Current browse context:\nL41: \nL42: math.AT\nL43: \nL44: cite16†< prev |   cite17†next > L45: \nL46: cite18†new | cite19†recent | cite20†2024-09 L47: \nL48: Change to browse by:\nL49: \nL50: cite21†math L51: cite22†math.GT L52: \nL5